# Copy to .env.local to override. Every value here is build-time (Vite) and is
# compiled into the bundle, so it is visible to anyone using the app. Do NOT put
# AWS credentials, secrets or private endpoints in this file.
#
# There is deliberately no mock or demo mode. The app talks to the real backend
# only, so what you see is always the result of a real scan.
#
# In normal use you do not need to set anything here. The app calls same-origin
# /api/*, and a signing tier holds the AWS credentials and signs each request:
#   - locally, that is the dev proxy (npm run devproxy), reached through the Vite
#     dev server proxy configured in vite.config.ts;
#   - in production, it is the web Lambda behind CloudFront, which signs with its
#     execution role.
# The browser therefore never holds a credential and never learns the API endpoint,
# which is why no API URL is configured below.

# Optional. Overrides the target the Vite dev server proxies /api to. Only useful
# if you run the local signing proxy on a different port.
# VITE_DEV_PROXY=http://127.0.0.1:8787
